testing/goldens — one committed cell grid per chrome surface

WHAT THESE ARE

Each file is `ktui_draw_dump()`'s output for one front end at one size: the
libktui cell buffer as plain text, every row padded to the full width, one
line per row. `testing/selftest.sh` renders the same frame and diffs.

WHY, BEYOND THE SHAPE CHECKS

selftest.sh asserts that a dump is SQUARE — every row the same width, enough
rows to be a box. That says nothing about CONTENT: a frame painted into the
wrong buffer, or diffed against a front buffer the commit has already swapped
away from, is the right width on every row and wrong on every row. A golden is
the only check that notices.

HOW TO REGENERATE

    KDOS_GOLDEN_UPDATE=1 testing/selftest.sh

then read the diff in `git diff testing/goldens/` before committing it. That
diff IS the review: it is a picture of what the change did to the screen.

THE RULE FOR ADDING ONE

A golden is committed only for a dump that is deterministic on ANY host — no
clock, no hostname, no readdir order, no absolute paths, nothing read out of
the developer's own /usr/share. Everything the surface reads comes from
`testing/fixtures/shell/` (`tree/` for the file chooser, `config/` for the
surfaces that parse an rc.xml or a comp.conf), frozen there on purpose so a
golden cannot move because somebody edited skel.

A surface that cannot meet that is left out and SAID SO in selftest.sh's
comment beside the list — cal draws the current month, the apps and places
menus read the host's /usr/share/applications and /proc/mounts, kdos-slit
renders the output of forked commands, the mixer enumerates the machine's ALSA
cards and kdos-users walks its password file. A golden pinned with a hack
nobody can reproduce is worse than a missing one.

Every dump is ASCII: `ktui_caps` is 0 with no terminal, so a surface drawing
straight to a buffer gets the ascii tier. A dump's tier follows whoever painted
it, not the fact that it is a dump. The rich and vt tiers are covered by the
ramp assertions in `src/libs/selftest.c`.

THE CELL FRAMES

`--dump-cells` — one line per non-blank cell, `row col U+XXXX fg bg attr` — is
the other half of the contract, and it is what makes a COLOUR regression
visible as well as a geometry one: a text frame is byte-identical across a
selection that stopped being an accent fill and a label that dropped to an
unreadable slot. The `cells-*.txt` files here are the frames that are
goldened, and they are fewer than the surfaces that implement the flag: a
frame is committed only where the same rule as above holds, and kdos-res and
the teams surface answer `--dump-cells` without one. A surface that is not
goldened is skipped by name rather than silently, so the list of what is
covered is the list of what was chosen.

